{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms","id":1546961,"title":"Adding phisical attributes to mechanisms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-14T05:44:46-08:00","id":1546961,"title":"Adding phisical attributes to mechanisms","content":"Increasing physical atributes is life acording to the rulebook. But what if its a mechanism? for example a mechanical arm or power armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:09:40-08:00","id":1546988,"title":"","content":"Depends a bit.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, improving the function of a mechanical device falls under Matter. Though depending on the issue it could be Entropy (stabilizing a highly experiment/temperamental design), Forces (the current device is needs more juice), Life (anything that's cybernetic can have problems on the flesh side of things), or Mind (again, body-machine interfacing, but on the mental integration side of things).<br /> <br /> That said, both of your examples aren't things that generally have &quot;Attributes.&quot; A suit of power armor doesn't usually have its own Stamina, it boosts your Soak rolls via an Armor rating, and movement via the vehicle rules, etc. Matter just bumps up how big of a bonus it provides, like Matter can give a cotton shirt the equivalent protection of a Kevlar vest. Robotic familiars and the like are what have Attributes to enhance, and when Matter would take over from what's normally done with Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:14:12-08:00","id":1546989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1546988#post1546988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends a bit.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, improving the function of a mechanical device falls under Matter. Though depending on the issue it could be Entropy (stabilizing a highly experiment/temperamental design), Forces (the current device is needs more juice), Life (anything that's cybernetic can have problems on the flesh side of things), or Mind (again, body-machine interfacing, but on the mental integration side of things).<br /> <br /> That said, both of your examples aren't things that generally have &quot;Attributes.&quot; A suit of power armor doesn't usually have its own Stamina, it boosts your Soak rolls via an Armor rating, and movement via the vehicle rules, etc. Matter just bumps up how big of a bonus it provides, like Matter can give a cotton shirt the equivalent protection of a Kevlar vest. Robotic familiars and the like are what have Attributes to enhance, and when Matter would take over from what's normally done with Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essencialy im trying to find out can you increse your physical atributes in other indirect ways that do not require life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:40:55-08:00","id":1546991,"title":"","content":"It's Mage, it depends on how you do it.<br /> <br /> If &quot;power armor&quot; is an instrument? No.<br /> <br /> If &quot;power armor&quot; is a Wonder where the magic is overcoming all the current technical limitations on why we can't build Iron Man armor, and while wearing it your Strength is considered 2 higher? Sure.<br /> <br /> If you have cybernetic implants? No, since those generally require Life and Matter, though someone else can install them for you. But that's also what the Enhancements Background is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:43:39-08:00","id":1546993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1546991#post1546991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If &quot;power armor&quot; is a Wonder where the magic is overcoming all the current technical limitations on why we can't build Iron Man armor, and while wearing it your Strength is considered 2 higher? Sure.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Again what spheres?<br /> We assume he has to create it<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:58:24-08:00","id":1546997,"title":"","content":"What do you want it to do? In what context?<br /> <br /> Building a functional version of the power-loader from Aliens that only needs to operate on VE Voidships is going to be a lot easier and require different Spheres, than trying to replicate the Iron Man suit (esp, all of the additional features Stark likes to tack on) that's going to fly around in normal reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T14:03:21-08:00","id":1546998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1546997#post1546997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you want it to do? In what context?<br /> <br /> Building a functional version of the power-loader from Aliens that only needs to operate on VE Voidships is going to be a lot easier and require different Spheres, than trying to replicate the Iron Man suit (esp, all of the additional features Stark likes to tack on) that's going to fly around in normal reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets say a medieval faithpowered armor that gives you +3 str cause it has its own str and moves with you and assists you (as a power armor concept should) as the topic suggests im only interested in the alternate increasing attributes part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T14:10:03-08:00","id":1547000,"title":"","content":"Faith doesn't matter, that's just Focus.<br /> <br /> I would require Forces, Matter, and because it's a Wonder Prime. Forces + Matter are the basics for building a &quot;living statue&quot; style magical construct, and you're just wearing it for extra strength instead of having an extra combatant around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T15:57:15-08:00","id":1547007,"title":"","content":"I'm going to take a look at material related to Iteration X, as this would probably be the best source. I haven't had occasion to look into this deeply, as I've never had a player create a character belonging to that group.<br /> <br /> Offhand, I'd probably require the use of <i>both </i>non-magickal skills <i>and </i>magick to design and create things like this. The character would be building the physical device, then using magick to alter or infuse it with properties which Consensus doesn't encompass. (The former step would be made easier if they're working from highly detailed blueprints and specifications, and not having to design it themselves.)<br /> <br /> In the case of physically integrated cybernetics, Life might still be necessary to prevent rejection, even if that takes the form of anti-rejection drugs which must be taken on occasion. Fusing a Matter pattern to a Life pattern seems like it would require some sort of ongoing stabilizing procedure. If it's a suit of armor you're talking about, Life might not be necessary if there's no physical interface, but Mind might then be used for purposes of user control (and tactile feedback, if that's required.) Creating a human machine interface by way of some sort of non-invasive &quot;mind scan&quot; alone would be very advanced stuff, and I'm not aware that the Technocracy has even prototyped anything like that yet.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, what you'd basically be doing is improving a mechanical device using magick, in such a way that it would give bonus dots or roll modifiers to physical attributes and tasks. Being Wonders by definition, you might use the same roles for enhancing physical attributes using Life, but using Matter in the place of Life, and necessitating technological skill to make it workable.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, the above sort of brings to mind the sorts of Sphere combinations necessary when trying to alter the physical patterns of vampires. I suppose that makes sense in the case of cybernetics, as you're dealing with some real grey areas between living and non-living patterns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T13:31:18-08:00","id":1547037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1546993#post1546993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again what spheres?<br /> We assume he has to create it</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go with Forces 2 and have it be a Wonder Power Armor.<br /> <br /> I would allow for it to improve Strength and/or Dexterity, but NOT Stamina. The Power Armor will have an armor rating for soaking thou. It will &quot;increase&quot; Strength by increasing your lifting, throwing or punching capabilities, not by increasing your own body's muscular capabilities. In essence, it's the Mecha doing the job, not the operator. The same goes for Dexterity, the Mecha gives extra speed, not the body.<br /> <br /> Stamina however is more than just soak dices, it implies cardiovascular capacity, which is exclusively about the user's body. It could theoretically be ingrained in the Power Armor, but it would have to be something like &quot;Integrated Stimpacks&quot; (from StarCraft) and it would need Life 3.<br /> <br /> I personally require Mind 1 for Dexterity, since I consider that Dexterity is a matter of reflexes rather than muscles and bones, thus for me Dexterity is in the mind, but that's my own personal headcannon. If you're not of the same opinion, then Forces 2 alone works for both Strength and Dexterity<br /> <br /> Edit: Entropy 2 can also be used instead of Forces 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T13:41:07-08:00","id":1547038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1546998#post1546998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lets say a medieval faithpowered armor that gives you +3 str cause it has its own str and moves with you and assists you (as a power armor concept should) as the topic suggests im only interested in the alternate increasing attributes part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm faithpowered?<br /> <br /> In that case I would go with Entropy 2, since the &quot;Divine will&quot; guiding destiny fits like a glove.<br /> <br /> For a techie power armor I would go with Forces 2.<br /> <br /> Both are equally valid mind you, you can make a +3Str &quot;Faitharmor&quot; with Forces 2 or a technological Power Armor with Entropy 2, but it's just more thematically fit to have it in the above manner","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T13:43:40-08:00","id":1547040,"title":"","content":"The more i play this game the more ideas pop up. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T13:50:44-08:00","id":1547043,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, you need Prime 3 or 4, depending on having Tass with appropriate resonance or not, to make them into wonders. I didn't mentioned that before because since they must be wonders, I assumed that would be implicit.<br /> <br /> I used &quot;Forged in the Dragon's Fire&quot; as my guide for building wonders, although I have my own house rules for it.<br /> <br /> Edit: with Mind 1 you can add any Social or Mental attributes in your &quot;Faithpowered&quot; wonder armor too (except for Appearance, which would be Entropy 4). But then it would actively &quot;change&quot; the user, rather than being exclusively intrinsic to the armor.<br /> <br /> PS: why Entropy 4 rather than Life 3 for Appearance?<br /> <br /> Because Appearance is incredibly subjective. &quot;Beauty is at the eyes of the beholder&quot;. Besides, let's assume we have a power to &quot;sculpt flesh&quot;, similar to the Tzimisce Vissicitude.<br /> <br /> How would we use it to make one more beautiful? Do we follow some &quot;facial symmetry&quot; theories? Some things are obvious - remove scars and marks, but some others aren't so much.<br /> <br /> Entropy 4 just bypasses that, since the universe itself will conspire to make you universally more appealing, rather than trying to adjust your appearance to what you yourself subjectively considers to be more appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 12-15-2024, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T16:02:05-08:00","id":1547046,"title":"","content":"I disagree that you can't use &quot;(Power) Armour&quot; as an Instrument. You definitely could, if it's part of your Focus. You would just need to manually cast all the Effects you wanted from it. (Though, if you wanted &quot;Power Armour&quot; to do a bunch of different things, you might want to make it a Wonder anyway, simply to have certain base functions available all the time).<br /> <br /> For the idea of gaining additional dots in Strength for the Faith user, the easiest and most straightforward WOULD just be to use Life 3. You're just using the armor as an Instrument to explain the situational buff to your stats. The other option would probably be to use Forces 3 (maybe with Prime 2) to manipulate and boost the power behind your movements, so you get an equivalent number of dots to Strength-based dice pools. You're not actually making yourself stronger, in terms of Attributes, but rather juicing the rolls you'd make with them.<br /> <br /> Matter 3 might be employed to strengthen the armor material itself, so it's harder and can resist deforming or breaking. As a ST, I might give you a reduced difficulty, as your armor acts as a brace. Taking more of the burden of the weight/force on itself. (Alternatively, you alter the physical properties of the material you're working against, so it's lighter or undergoes less friction, though the latter might be done with Forces 2 instead). But an Effect alone wouldn't make YOU stronger (wouldn't give you more dots to the dice pool).<br /> <br /> (Come to think of it, Matter 3 could alternatively be used as a sort of dynamic transformation. Much how someone would reshape stone into a spike to impale someone as an attack, you could reshape the armor so it moves and deforms with extra power behind it. So...possibly?)<br /> <br /> You might be able to use Matter 4 to effectively incorporate machinery into the armor (shrinking it to fit in the space) that could do the mechanical work more efficiently. But I don't know if a Faith user that isn't also using some kind of technomantic Practice could swing that, especially in pre-modern times or without the appropriate Abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T20:57:03-08:00","id":1547048,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, my &quot;no&quot; regarding armor-as-instrument was to it allowing you to circumvent Life to boost your physical Attributes. While you can also use a Wonder as an instrument as well, normal instruments don't do anything magical, the mage does. If you're wearing normal armor and call on faith to give you strength, it's just using your Focus to use Life 3. Wearing the armor doesn't justify other Spheres to increase your stats by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T03:18:56-08:00","id":1547052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1547046#post1547046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree that you can't use &quot;(Power) Armour&quot; as an Instrument. You definitely could, if it's part of your Focus. You would just need to manually cast all the Effects you wanted from it. (Though, if you wanted &quot;Power Armour&quot; to do a bunch of different things, you might want to make it a Wonder anyway, simply to have certain base functions available all the time).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you absolutely could cast effects through the &quot;power armor&quot;, having it as a focus. I just thought that OP wanted a wonder by the way he structured his question<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the idea of gaining additional dots in Strength for the Faith user, the easiest and most straightforward WOULD just be to use Life 3. You're just using the armor as an Instrument to explain the situational buff to your stats. The other option would probably be to use Forces 3 (maybe with Prime 2) to manipulate and boost the power behind your movements, so you get an equivalent number of dots to Strength-based dice pools. You're not actually making yourself stronger, in terms of Attributes, but rather juicing the rolls you'd make with them. </div> </div> </div>I just have a minor disagreement here about the use of Forces. In this case, it would be Forces 2. Forces 2 is what regulates the intensity of any given energy type. If you want to amplify or damper any sort of energy, that's Forces 2. Therefore, for &quot;Strength&quot;, the intent being clearly to amplify the amount of energy that the body can apply - so for example, if I try to lift something heavy, then I'll want Forces to give a little extra energy for that effort, but also would I want a little bit extra energy for when I'm punching someone's face - then all of that would be Forces 2.<br /> <br /> I know why people gets confused, and that's because we think with a real world physics's mind. We are thinking that, in this case, by adding energy to the system we are &quot;creating energy out of nothing&quot;. And such assertion would be right for the real world, but is not the case for Mage the Ascension. The &quot;intensity&quot; of energy in MtA is not a matter of increasing electrons to a system, thus requiring the creation of extra stuff. &quot;Intensity&quot; instead is just a matter of perception. And &quot;intensity&quot; is controlled entirely by Forces 2, not 3.<br /> <br /> What Forces 3 thus is to change one type of energy into another, it's the &quot;alchemical transmutation&quot; of Forces. Thus, it is changing movement into electricity for instance.<br /> <br /> And, if you're invoking fireballs from the ether, then you need Prime 2 and a single point of Quint, because you're summoning fireballs out of nothing, thus you're transmuting Quint into fire energy. But Forces 3 is always and exclusively only transmutation, remember that.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Matter 3 might be employed to strengthen the armor material itself, so it's harder and can resist deforming or breaking. As a ST, I might give you a reduced difficulty, as your armor acts as a brace. Taking more of the burden of the weight/force on itself. (Alternatively, you alter the physical properties of the material you're working against, so it's lighter or undergoes less friction, though the latter might be done with Forces 2 instead). But an Effect alone wouldn't make YOU stronger (wouldn't give you more dots to the dice pool). </div> </div> </div>Matter 3 could change your Egyptian cotton suit into Kevlar, but you require Matter 5 to change properties rather than just transmuting *existing* materials.<br /> <br /> Besides, there's nothing really that Matter can do other than giving extra armor soaking dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Come to think of it, Matter 3 could alternatively be used as a sort of dynamic transformation. Much how someone would reshape stone into a spike to impale someone as an attack, you could reshape the armor so it moves and deforms with extra power behind it. So...possibly?) </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that would be like Wolverine-ing into the fight. In game mechanics, not different from adding damage such as a sword would.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You might be able to use Matter 4 to effectively incorporate machinery into the armor (shrinking it to fit in the space) that could do the mechanical work more efficiently. But I don't know if a Faith user that isn't also using some kind of technomantic Practice could swing that, especially in pre-modern times or without the appropriate Abilities. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but what would that &quot;machinery&quot; actually do? Is it mundane or magical &quot;machinery&quot;? If it's mundane then it must be very well explained and justified; if it is magical, then we are just back at square one and necessitating the descriptions of spheres for whatever effects said &quot;machinery&quot; applies on the overall armour.<br /> <br /> For instance, &quot;integrated neuron-circuits&quot; could be &quot;machinery&quot; in the form of &quot;quantum chips&quot; (or whatever technobabble of your choice) integrated into the helmet of the wearer, which is a technology that stimulates neurons, thus having an integrated Mind 1 effect that increases Social And/Or Mental attributes of the wearer. That could be a wonder, or it could be just the mambo jumbery excuse for the instrument of the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T03:23:47-08:00","id":1547053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1547048#post1547048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, my &quot;no&quot; regarding armor-as-instrument was to it allowing you to circumvent Life to boost your physical Attributes. While you can also use a Wonder as an instrument as well, normal instruments don't do anything magical, the mage does. If you're wearing normal armor and call on faith to give you strength, it's just using your Focus to use Life 3. Wearing the armor doesn't justify other Spheres to increase your stats by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sphere itself justifies it. You don't actually need a set of armor to use Forces 2 to make yourself &quot;stronger&quot;, to make your feeble arms capable of lifting heavy stuff or to make your tiny hands deliver supernaturally potent blows. You just simply Abracadabra the Forces of your feeble body and voil\u00e1, it is done.<br /> <br /> Likewise, you don't need a armor for using Entropy in the same manner. You just Abracadabra the universe into conspiring in your favor to do so.<br /> <br /> Edit: the difference from Life 3 is that you're not actually getting stronger, you're just &quot;making things easier for your own strength&quot;. You're not increasing your muscular capacity to smash stuff, you're just adding extra external juicy to your own natural smashing capabilities.<br /> <br /> The practical effect ends up being the same thou, only the method differs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 12-16-2024, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T06:21:10-08:00","id":1547056,"title":"","content":"Where I could see using Matter to increase physical stats is if the mage used a Life/Matter spell to turn himself into a robot or a mobile bronze statue, or something like that. After that, if he wanted to raise his strength or durability, Matter would be the correct sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T13:27:58-08:00","id":1547066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1547052#post1547052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have a minor disagreement here about the use of Forces. In this case, it would be Forces 2. Forces 2 is what regulates the intensity of any given energy type. If you want to amplify or damper any sort of energy, that's Forces 2. Therefore, for &quot;Strength&quot;, the intent being clearly to amplify the amount of energy that the body can apply - so for example, if I try to lift something heavy, then I'll want Forces to give a little extra energy for that effort, but also would I want a little bit extra energy for when I'm punching someone's face - then all of that would be Forces 2.<br /> <br /> I know why people gets confused, and that's because we think with a real world physics's mind. We are thinking that, in this case, by adding energy to the system we are &quot;creating energy out of nothing&quot;. And such assertion would be right for the real world, but is not the case for Mage the Ascension. The &quot;intensity&quot; of energy in MtA is not a matter of increasing electrons to a system, thus requiring the creation of extra stuff. &quot;Intensity&quot; instead is just a matter of perception. And &quot;intensity&quot; is controlled entirely by Forces 2, not 3.<br /> <br /> What Forces 3 thus is to change one type of energy into another, it's the &quot;alchemical transmutation&quot; of Forces. Thus, it is changing movement into electricity for instance.<br /> <br /> And, if you're invoking fireballs from the ether, then you need Prime 2 and a single point of Quint, because you're summoning fireballs out of nothing, thus you're transmuting Quint into fire energy. But Forces 3 is always and exclusively only transmutation, remember that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fundamentally disagree with your reading, vis a vis what Forces 2 can do. Checking both Mage Revised and M20, Forces 2 is described as manipulating and dampening forces, but <i>not amplifying</i> them. (Except in M20 for sound, weirdly). You can't make them stronger, because that means adding more of the force in question to the system.<br /> <br /> This is why I specified Forces 3, and possible +Prime 2, for use in this &quot;Strength boosting&quot; effect. With Forces 2, you can perhaps manipulate the kinetic forces at play to more efficiently employ the strength you already have. Effectively, lower the difficulty of the roll. To actually ADD DICE to the pool, you can't just rely on that existing force. You have to add more of it to the system. Either using Forces 3 on its own to siphon other elements and turn them into &quot;Strength&quot;, or add Prime 2 to create the extra power ex nihilo.<br /> <br /> While the game makes much ado about not adhering too closely to physics as we know it, the way the rules are laid out and described in practice still takes many cues from &quot;scientific&quot; understandings of energy. You can dissipate or stop forces with Forces 2, but you generally can't make them STRONGER without Forces 3. At best, you can concentrate or direct what's already there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T13:47:26-08:00","id":1547067,"title":"","content":"&quot;Although she cannot conjure energies just yet, the mage<br /> may now alter the flow of existing forces. Sound can be muted<br /> or amplified; shadows can be gathered, shaped, or dispelled.<br /> The mage can warp light to make things invisible, change their<br /> colors by altering the spectrum of localized light, or render them<br /> silent by bending sound waves in their vicinity. With a wave of<br /> her hand, she can disrupt electrical currents; flare flames; or<br /> direct the course of winds, momentum, or gravity.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would assume that all of the examples no matter if its electricity, shadows, light or fire can be dampened or amplified in this description. I would even say that &quot;flare flames&quot; is an example of amplifying flames.<br /> Its the same as with matter there is no rule of conserving mass or size when transforming one matter to another.<br /> <br /> Then again we have in Forces 3:<br /> <br /> &quot;Now the mage can alter and invoke the energies she could<br /> only touch before. By adding Prime 2, she may conjure winds,<br /> fire, electricity, gravitational wells, and so forth. Combining<br /> this Rank with Life or Matter, she can transform people into<br /> electricity (Life 5/ Forces 3); change water into air (Forces 3/<br /> Matter 3), or attach elemental force to material forms \u2013 making<br /> them fly, pinning them to the ground, and having other, similar<br /> effects (generally with Life or Matter 3). And by adding an<br /> ephemeral Sphere to this Rank, she might erode or enhance<br /> energies (Entropy 3); manifest thoughts into energies (Mind 3);<br /> transmute spirit-stuff into physical energies (Spirit 3); or set<br /> triggers for energy fluctuations at some later interval (Time 4).&quot;<br /> <br /> I find this one wierd cause for once its saying that transforming water into air is forces (not important in this dicsusion it just bothers me). And that energies can be dampened or enhanced only with the help of enropy. I have no words for this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 12-16-2024, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T14:13:50-08:00","id":1547072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1547066#post1547066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fundamentally disagree with your reading, vis a vis what Forces 2 can do. Checking both Mage Revised and M20, Forces 2 is described as manipulating and dampening forces, but <i>not amplifying</i> them. (Except in M20 for sound, weirdly). You can't make them stronger, because that means adding more of the force in question to the system.<br /> <br /> This is why I specified Forces 3, and possible +Prime 2, for use in this &quot;Strength boosting&quot; effect. With Forces 2, you can perhaps manipulate the kinetic forces at play to more efficiently employ the strength you already have. Effectively, lower the difficulty of the roll. To actually ADD DICE to the pool, you can't just rely on that existing force. You have to add more of it to the system. Either using Forces 3 on its own to siphon other elements and turn them into &quot;Strength&quot;, or add Prime 2 to create the extra power ex nihilo.<br /> <br /> While the game makes much ado about not adhering too closely to physics as we know it, the way the rules are laid out and described in practice still takes many cues from &quot;scientific&quot; understandings of energy. You can dissipate or stop forces with Forces 2, but you generally can't make them STRONGER without Forces 3. At best, you can concentrate or direct what's already there.</div> </div> </div> </div>On page 420, Forces 2 can add velocity to a thrown attack. This comes again on 422 for any attack.<br /> <br /> On 464, Forces (with no mention of Prime) is suggested for boosting the effects of a taser.<br /> <br /> Speed and slow velocity is Forces 2+ according to pg 509. (The + has to do with needing higher ranks to slow larger areas/objects.)<br /> <br /> Forces 2 is also the rank for flight, levitation, and telekinesis, all of which are quite capable of accelerating something, and indeed, wouldn't work if they didn't.<br /> <br /> Most directly, the Forces 2 writeup specifically mentions amplifying sound, flaring flames, and gathering and dispelling shadows. So I would say that rank 2 is clearly capable of amplification. <br /> <br /> Also, if we are going to take a cue from science on this, amplifying and muting forces should be treated the same way. Energy can neither be created nor destroyed and all that. <br /> <br /> The better way of understanding Forces, I would say, is that if the forces pattern already exists you can manipulate it, amplify it, or suppress it with Forces 2. You don't need Forces 3 unless you are changing it from one type of Force into another, and you don't need Prime 2 unless you are creating the pattern entirely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T14:28:28-08:00","id":1547073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1547053#post1547053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't actually need a set of armor to use Forces 2 to make yourself &quot;stronger&quot;, to make your feeble arms capable of lifting heavy stuff or to make your tiny hands deliver supernaturally potent blows. You just simply Abracadabra the Forces of your feeble body and voil\u00e1, it is done.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm in agreement that Forces 2 is all you need to amplify a single Forces Pattern, I do not agree that Forces 2 can, as written and by itself, replicate increased Strength (what quelsec actually asked for) as a mechanical effect. Forces 2 should either be reducing difficulties (as per Magic Enhancing Abilities) or just like your argument for Stamina, only be providing extra dice to damage.<br /> <br /> Wonder armor that is enchanted to amplify the power of your strikes would be Forces 2 and increase your damage dice by effectively giving you a better &quot;weapon.&quot; Simple, basic, classic stuff there. Doing everything that +X Strength would do is a separate matter. Grappling, lifting and carrying objects/Feats of Strength, jumping would all be different effects under the Forces 2 umbrella; which is theoretically possible but hardly practical Wonder design. <br /> <br /> This also ignores the part of this where we're trying to create something that falls under the concept of &quot;power armor&quot; that's more than just armor-as-instrument. If the armor itself is doing work, the armor itself needs energy. Plate mail doesn't have energy to do work beyond some potential energy to fall if dropped. You exert energy to move it around, because it's worth it for the protection it provides. If the plate mail Wonder is actually doing (at least some of) the work (ala power armor) rather than just amplifying your own energetic outputs, you need Matter combined with Forces to make the inanimate animate. The point of having a more technologically advanced base that already has mechanical components would be to get around needing Matter directly (you'd probably still need Matter to make the components because we don't have practical ones IRL for this but they don't need to be full Wonders, just specially prepared materials), but that runs the risk of upping the required to Forces 3 because you're going to burn through your batteries without magical levels of power generation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise, you don't need a armor for using Entropy in the same manner. You just Abracadabra the universe into conspiring in your favor to do so. </div> </div> </div>I have no interest in debating your headcanon on what Entropy can do; but as far as I can tell that's all you're offering here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: the difference from Life 3 is that you're not actually getting stronger, you're just &quot;making things easier for your own strength&quot;. You're not increasing your muscular capacity to smash stuff, you're just adding extra external juicy to your own natural smashing capabilities.<br /> <br /> The practical effect ends up being the same thou, only the method differs </div> </div> </div>The issue is that the practical effect doesn't end up being the same (+X Strength as the effect of activating the Wonder/wearing it if it's always on). Forces 2 (or even for what Entropy 2 can do) would be -X difficulty or +X dice in select circumstances (again, just like your statements about not being able to add Stamina, just increase Soak).<br /> <br /> Your own phrasing, while perhaps intended for comedic effect, is still telling: &quot;smash.&quot; The sample is focused completely on damage, not everything Strength does in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T20:34:07-08:00","id":1547087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1547073#post1547073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'm in agreement that Forces 2 is all you need to amplify a single Forces Pattern, I do not agree that Forces 2 can, as written and by itself, replicate increased Strength (what quelsec actually asked for) as a mechanical effect. Forces 2 should either be reducing difficulties (as per Magic Enhancing Abilities) or just like your argument for Stamina, only be providing extra dice to damage.<br /> <br /> Wonder armor that is enchanted to amplify the power of your strikes would be Forces 2 and increase your damage dice by effectively giving you a better &quot;weapon.&quot; Simple, basic, classic stuff there. Doing everything that +X Strength would do is a separate matter. Grappling, lifting and carrying objects/Feats of Strength, jumping would all be different effects under the Forces 2 umbrella; which is theoretically possible but hardly practical Wonder design.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things that Forces does is control movement. Kinetic energy, movement. And the lvl 2 of Forces allows you to amplify or damper it at will.<br /> <br /> Lifting something is movement. Punching someone is also movement. Jumping is also movement.<br /> <br /> You can use Forces 2 to amplify ALL kinetic energy from your body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This also ignores the part of this where we're trying to create something that falls under the concept of &quot;power armor&quot; that's more than just armor-as-instrument. If the armor itself is doing work, the armor itself needs energy. Plate mail doesn't have energy to do work beyond some potential energy to fall if dropped. You exert energy to move it around, because it's worth it for the protection it provides. If the plate mail Wonder is actually doing (at least some of) the work (ala power armor) rather than just amplifying your own energetic outputs, you need Matter combined with Forces to make the inanimate animate. The point of having a more technologically advanced base that already has mechanical components would be to get around needing Matter directly (you'd probably still need Matter to make the components because we don't have practical ones IRL for this but they don't need to be full Wonders, just specially prepared materials), but that runs the risk of upping the required to Forces 3 because you're going to burn through your batteries without magical levels of power generation. </div> </div> </div>As for the &quot;Power Armor&quot; sure, you could place a battery of some kind, but that's not necessary. An Etherite could build one based entirely on Hydraulics, like in the movie &quot;Crazy Adventures of Johnny West&quot; or something, which has a giant spider mecha that uses hydraulics in the 19th century. The &quot;source&quot; of the energy will be the very kinetic energy of the body of the user. <br /> Not my fault you can't understand the most basic concepts of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have no interest in debating your headcanon on what Entropy can do; but as far as I can tell that's all you're offering here. </div> </div> </div>And I have no interest in debating on what is the headcanon of someone that clearly have zero comprehensive skills of what Entropy does, so your silence is doing everybody a favor here, thank you very much for that. I only wish you would exercise your skill to remain silent a bit more, you can be sure that the entire forum would benefit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue is that the practical effect doesn't end up being the same (+X Strength as the effect of activating the Wonder/wearing it if it's always on). Forces 2 (or even for what Entropy 2 can do) would be -X difficulty or +X dice in select circumstances (again, just like your statements about not being able to add Stamina, just increase Soak).<br /> <br /> Your own phrasing, while perhaps intended for comedic effect, is still telling: &quot;smash.&quot; The sample is focused completely on damage, not everything Strength does in the game. </div> </div> </div>And your own phrasing shows your complete lack of reading skills. Go back to the books and read them again, because you clearly didn't understand anything. Forces can increase ANY kinetic energy. That is NOT just simply adjusting difficulty. Heck, you can even use Forces 2 to LEVITATE things, let alone reduce the necessary Strength to lift something - or lifting yourself (aka &quot;jumping&quot;).<br /> <br /> As for Entropy, Entropy 2 CAN add extra dices to activities, it's NOT just adjusting difficulty. Go read it again, you're desperate needing it. Don't expect me to all quote everything from the books every time you're saying something stupid.<br /> <br /> I would say thou, that using Entropy 2 to lift stuff may be stretching it to the limit, but it is neither said to not be possible anywhere and it is not entirely impossible to envision either. For instance, during competitive lifting, sometimes we see the competitor struggling and failing, and sometimes we see that he almost had it... Then, a lucky push could be all that he needed to succeed - hence where Entropy enters.<br /> <br /> As for punching, throwing or jumping, there's a factor of randomness - and thus of &quot;luck&quot; - that is much more present <br /> <br /> Go read &quot;Lucky Shot&quot; from revised, like I said, I'm not your nanny to be doing your homework every time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T20:49:08-08:00","id":1547088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546961-adding-phisical-attributes-to-mechanisms?p=1547066#post1547066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fundamentally disagree with your reading, vis a vis what Forces 2 can do. Checking both Mage Revised and M20, Forces 2 is described as manipulating and dampening forces, but <i>not amplifying</i> them. (Except in M20 for sound, weirdly). You can't make them stronger, because that means adding more of the force in question to the system.<br /> <br /> This is why I specified Forces 3, and possible +Prime 2, for use in this &quot;Strength boosting&quot; effect. With Forces 2, you can perhaps manipulate the kinetic forces at play to more efficiently employ the strength you already have. Effectively, lower the difficulty of the roll. To actually ADD DICE to the pool, you can't just rely on that existing force. You have to add more of it to the system. Either using Forces 3 on its own to siphon other elements and turn them into &quot;Strength&quot;, or add Prime 2 to create the extra power ex nihilo.<br /> <br /> While the game makes much ado about not adhering too closely to physics as we know it, the way the rules are laid out and described in practice still takes many cues from &quot;scientific&quot; understandings of energy. You can dissipate or stop forces with Forces 2, but you generally can't make them STRONGER without Forces 3. At best, you can concentrate or direct what's already there.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that may very well be the case, it would be a case upon which the writers contradict themselves, since it is very well established that something like Light vs Darkness is a matter of Paradigm rather than rl physics, and I use that exact example because it is the example given on first edition, second edition and revised.<br /> <br /> It clearly states that &quot;darkness is not necessarily the absence of light&quot;. It also gives the example about &quot;Cold vs Hot&quot;. That, for a technocratic paradigm, cold would be the &quot;absence of heat&quot;, but for a mystic this would not be so, being instead it's opposite - thus implying that a Techie can turn Light into Darkness with Forces 2, but a Mystic would need Forces 3.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, there's no distinction in terms of Quintessence between a 3 amperes current and a 300 one. Quintessence is &quot;subjective potential&quot;. You won't find anywhere, for instance, something like &quot;you need 1 quintessence for every 50kg/100 pounds of summoned matter&quot;. The reason being that quintessence is an ephemeral quality, not something that is quantifiable in a material sense.<br /> <br /> Thus, there's really no difference in the ephemeral terms of Quintessence between applying 5 joules of pressure or 500 joules of pressure in a punch, unless this somehow possess some metaphysical quality of its own.<br /> <br /> The same single point of Quintessence would be needed for summoning a small spark to light a candle, or to invoke a huge fireball the size of a man.<br /> <br /> It does then stands to reason that amplifying a Force is just a mere matter of control, thus being Forces 2. And in that point, I have to tell you that MtA is NOT an Universe upon which the law of conservation of mass and energy is applicable.<br /> <br /> MtA is a Gnostic universe, upon which everything is a &quot;dream of the Demiurge&quot;. It follows Kant's Immaterialism. Not rl physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T18:16:34-08:00","id":1547127,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Reminder: Please keep it civil, folks. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-19T06:43:25-08:00","id":1547147,"title":"","content":"Found what I was looking for in regards to augmenting physical attributes using hypertech.<br /> <br /> The Iteration X convention book has some systems advice on this, and refers heavily to the Enhancement background when it comes to cybernetics, which differs somewhat in M20. The latter is not for the faint of heart systems-wise. Using hypertech doesn't dodge the permanent Paradox which comes of using magick to enhance Attributes to &quot;unnatural&quot; levels, and there are some <i>very </i>nasty things Life adepts can do to those who graft mechanisms onto their bodies, provided they sufficiently understand what they're dealing with. Those primium countermeasures the Conventions developed are the main defense cyborgs have against being hit with magickally induced rejection of their own implants and grafted prosthetics, and if those fail it can get pretty grisly.<br /> <br /> In the realm of stuff like armored suits, there are some good examples given in the Iteration X book, and it'd be pretty easy to work off those in order to come up with variants. That material was written for Revised, so some tweaking might be necessary to get it to fit with M20 rules.<br /> <br /> In crossover games involving wraiths, Artificers are probably the deadliest threat those using Technocracy hypertech of any sort can come up against. The paradigms, methods and tools of the Conventions provide for no particular defense against the Inhabit Arcanos. On the other hand, such restless would we well warned not to try the same tricks against Tradition technomancers. There are some pretty entertaining examples of what can go wrong when a wraith tries to Inhabit mad Science devices..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}